            <ArticleTitle>Factors associated with preventable out-of-hospital nontraumatic cardiac arrest.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1244-7, A6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To identify ways to decrease the risk of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (CA) caused by an acute coronary syndrome, we examined factors associated with the development of CA &gt; or = 1 hour after symptom onset. Multivariate analysis revealed that a low level of physical activity, a history of diabetes mellitus, and a history of unstable angina are associated with out-of-hospital CA occurring &gt; or = hour after symptom onset.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
